# What `gcloud builds submit` uploads as the build source.
#
# This file exists mostly so the upload is predictable: without it, gcloud
# generates a .gcloudignore from .gitignore and writes it into the checkout,
# which is a surprising side effect of running a build.
#
# It is deliberately short. The Docker build applies `.dockerignore` on top of
# whatever arrives, so the finer trimming of the build context already happens
# there; the only things worth keeping out of the upload itself are the ones
# that must not travel or would make it large. `Dockerfile` must stay — Cloud
# Build reads it from the uploaded source.

# History, not source: by far the largest thing in the checkout.
.git

# Local secrets and local state.
.env
data/

# Build and test artifacts.
*.test
*.out
coverage.*
*.coverprofile
profile.cov
test-output.json
